WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
Slow becomes slowly.

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.990
In English you just tack on the letters L,

3
00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:08.810
Y. French has «lent», meaning slow.

4
00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.760
So how do you get from there to slowly?

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.110
Then there's better.

6
00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.050
«Ce livre est meilleur.»
This book is better.

7
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:19.250
Simple. But what about I read better now?

8
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:23.120
Is that «meilleur» too, or
something else entirely?

9
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.080
So how do you turn slow into slowly,

10
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.960
and why is better
sometimes not «meilleur»?

11
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.800
In this mission, you'll run
adjectives along a conveyor

12
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.700
belt and see what comes out.

13
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.670
Then you'll drop adverbs
into sentences in the lab,

14
00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.360
and find out where they belong.

15
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.680
Your mission: work out how
French builds an adverb,

16
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.960
and when better isn't «meilleur».
